<exercise xml:id="recursive-binary-splitting-first-cut">
  <introduction>
    <p>Use recursive binary splitting and the shown figure to answer the following questions. Complete the tables for each part, and use them to justify your answer in each case.</p>    
    <image source="figures/recursive_binary_splitting_first_cut">
      <shortdescription>Predictor-space diagrams for identifying the first cut using recursive binary splitting.</shortdescription>
    </image>
    </introduction>
    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
           Identify the first cut in the classification tree (a).         
        </p>
        <table>
        <title>Recursive binary splitting errors for classification tree.</title>
          <tabular>
            <row><cell>Splits</cell><cell>Error</cell><cell>Splits</cell><cell>Error</cell></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{11}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{21}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{12}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{22}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{13}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{23}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{14}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{24}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{15}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{25}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{16}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{26}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{17}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{27}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{18}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{28}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell/><cell/><cell><m>s_{29}</m></cell><cell/></row>
          </tabular>
        </table>
      </statement>
      <hint>
        <p>For classification, use the splitting error
  <md>
  \text{E}_s = \frac{N_{\text{left}}}{N} \times E_{\text{left}} + \frac{N_{\text{right}}}{N} \times E_{\text{right}}
</md>
where <m>N</m> is the number of points in the parent node, <m>N_{\text{left}}</m> and <m>N_{\text{right}}</m> are the number of points in the left and right child nodes, respectively. <m>E_{\text{left}}</m> and <m>E_{\text{right}}</m> are the classification errors for the left and right child nodes, respectively.   </p>
</hint>
    </task>
    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Identify the first cut in the regression tree (b) using the data given in the table below. 
        </p>

    <table>
    <title>Training Data for part (b).</title>       
      <tabular>
        <row>
          <cell><m>i</m></cell>
          <cell><m>Y_i</m></cell>
          <cell><m>i</m></cell>
          <cell><m>Y_i</m></cell>
        </row>
        <row><cell>1</cell><cell>7.5</cell><cell>6</cell><cell>9.8</cell></row>
        <row><cell>2</cell><cell>8.8</cell><cell>7</cell><cell>7.1</cell></row>
        <row><cell>3</cell><cell>6</cell><cell>8</cell><cell>8.5</cell></row>
        <row><cell>4</cell><cell>9.4</cell><cell>9</cell><cell>8.3</cell></row>
        <row><cell>5</cell><cell>7.8</cell><cell>10</cell><cell>9.2</cell></row>
      </tabular>
    </table>
      


        <table>
        <title>Recursive binary splitting errors for regression tree.</title>
          <tabular>
            <row><cell>Splits</cell><cell>Error</cell><cell>Splits</cell><cell>Error</cell></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{11}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{21}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{12}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{22}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{13}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{23}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{14}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{24}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{15}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{25}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{16}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{26}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{17}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{27}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell><m>s_{18}</m></cell><cell/><cell><m>s_{28}</m></cell><cell/></row>
            <row><cell/><cell/><cell><m>s_{29}</m></cell><cell/></row>
          </tabular>
        </table>
              </statement>
              <hint>
                <p>
For regression, use the RSS splitting error.
                </p>
              </hint>
    </task>


  
</exercise>

<exercise xml:id="oob-classification-error">
  <statement>
    <p>Compute the Out-Of-Bag (OOB) error. If you need to split the predictors' space, use a tree with one level. In case of a tie when splitting along either <m>X_1</m> or <m>X_2</m>, break the tie by splitting <m>X_1</m>.</p>
    
    <image source="figures/OOB_error_classification" width="85%">
      <shortdescription>Classification data and tree information for computing the out-of-bag error.</shortdescription>
    </image>
  </statement>
</exercise>

<exercise xml:id="oob-regression-error">
  <statement>
    <p>Compute the Out-Of-Bag (OOB) error using the data given in the table below. If you need to split the predictors' space, use a tree with one level. In case of a tie when splitting along either <m>X_1</m> or <m>X_2</m>, break the tie by splitting <m>X_1</m>.</p>
    <image source="figures/OOB_error_regression" width="85%">
      <shortdescription>Regression data and tree information for computing the out-of-bag error.</shortdescription>
    </image>
    <table>
    <title>Training Data.</title>    
      <tabular>
        <row><cell><m>i</m></cell><cell><m>Y_i</m></cell></row>
        <row><cell>1</cell><cell>3.4</cell></row>
        <row><cell>2</cell><cell>6.2</cell></row>
        <row><cell>3</cell><cell>7</cell></row>
        <row><cell>4</cell><cell>8.3</cell></row>
        <row><cell>5</cell><cell>4.1</cell></row>
        <row><cell>6</cell><cell>10.1</cell></row>
        <row><cell>7</cell><cell>9.5</cell></row>
      </tabular>
    </table>    
  </statement>
</exercise>



<exercise xml:id="random-forest-first-second-splits">
  <statement>
    <p>Using random forests, draw the first and second splits using the first two random numbers in the shown table for each split.</p>    
    <sidebyside widths="65% 35%">
      <image source="figures/random_forests_splitting">
        <shortdescription>Predictor space for drawing the first and second splits in a random forest.</shortdescription>
      </image>
      <table>
      <title>Random Numbers for each split.</title>      
        <tabular>
          <row>
            <cell>Split</cell>
            <cell>Random number generator on <m>\{1,2\}</m></cell>
          </row>
          <row><cell>1</cell><cell>2</cell></row>
          <row><cell>2</cell><cell>1</cell></row>
          <row><cell>3</cell><cell>2</cell></row>
          <row><cell>4</cell><cell>2</cell></row>
          <row><cell>5</cell><cell>1</cell></row>
        </tabular>
      </table>
    </sidebyside>
  </statement>
  <hint>
    <p>
      Use the classification splitting error formula to determine the best split at each step.
    </p>
  </hint>
</exercise>
